        "system": {
          "description": "<p>A so-called &ldquo;fur coat&rdquo; is outerwear made from a living primitive organism. The creature&rsquo;s skin, fur, or scales are real. The organism is cultivated from transgenic stocks and grown around molds into clothing shapes, often with actual usefulness: polar bear parkas, seal diving suits, porcupine coats, etc. Fur coats are modified with wireless controls and haptic systems, so they can be made to move, shiver, massage, or prickle up on command.</p>",
